{"_id":"68a736218ec3d8323af191b3","nodeId":"eKtdDtiJygKQ4PuEylFQY","roadmapSlug":"java","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:13.404Z","description":"# Map\n\nA Map is a data structure that stores data in key-value pairs. Each key is unique, and it maps to a specific value. Think of it like a dictionary where you use a word (the key) to look up its definition (the value). Maps allow you to efficiently retrieve, add, or remove values based on their associated keys.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Generic Map in Java","url":"https://jenkov.com/tutorials/java-generics/generic-map.html","_id":"692485f1467651eddb4d33bb"},{"type":"article","title":"Java Map","url":"https://jenkov.com/tutorials/java-collections/map.html","_id":"692485f1467651eddb4d33bc"},{"type":"article","title":"Java ConcurrentMap","url":"https://jenkov.com/tutorials/java-util-concurrent/concurrentmap.html","_id":"692485f1467651eddb4d33bd"},{"type":"article","title":"Java SortedMap","url":"https://jenkov.com/tutorials/java-collections/sortedmap.html","_id":"692485f1467651eddb4d33be"}],"updatedAt":"2025-11-24T16:21:05.627Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04defb5fcb94d0416bad","title":"DataCamp - Java Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbYnP9"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/java/content/eKtdDtiJygKQ4PuEylFQY.md"}